Week 5 Secure Pipline with mTLS PDF
- Connection time will be measurably slower with mTLS. The extra certificate exchange adds a round-trip plus verification time. On a local machine, this might be 5-20 milliseconds extra. On a remote connection, it could be more.
- Message latency (after the connection is established) should be nearly identical. Once the TLS handshake completes, both one-way TLS and mTLS use the same encrypted channel. The handshake is a one-time cost per connection, not per message.
- Think of it like entering a building. With one-way TLS, the guard checks your badge and waves you through. With mTLS, the guard checks your badge and you verify the guard's ID before entering. It takes a few extra seconds at the door — but once you're inside, you walk at the same speed either way.

