Connection time +30%
~7 ms extra
- Devices connect once and stay connected. This cost is paid once per session, not per message.
Message latency +5%
~0.2 ms extra
- Sensor readings every 5 seconds. A fraction-of-a-millisecond delay is invisible.
Leak detection
No change
- Leaks take minutes to develop. Millisecond differences don't affect detection.

-mTLS adds overhead to connection setup (extra certificate exchange), not to message delivery
-Connection overhead is a one-time cost — devices connect once and stay connected for hours
-Message latency should be nearly identical between TLS and mTLS
-Context matters more than percentages — 30% of 24ms is still only 7ms
